# This package ships a file literally named .gitignore (it is git's global
# core.excludesfile). Stow's *built-in* ignore list contains `\.gitignore`, so
# without this file ~/.gitignore is silently never linked and core.excludesfile
# points at nothing. Defining any .stow-local-ignore replaces that built-in
# list, so the safe defaults are restored here — minus .gitignore.
\.git
\.stow-local-ignore
CVS
.+~
\#.*\#
